# Bloom Blast — hard rules (all age groups)

## Never touch finished levels

- Only change the **current level** the user is discussing.
- Do **not** edit levels already approved unless the user reopens that level.
- **Groups 1 and 2 are finished** — do not edit Tiny Explorers (L1–5) or Curious Minds (L6–10) content, glyphs, voice, or gestures unless the user reopens them.
- Group 1 controls stay **drag / tap-swap** as built — do not convert Group 1 to swipe.

## Group 2 & Group 3 — swipe

- Primary input: **finger swipe** to an adjacent box to swap (modern kids match-3).
- Backup: tap one box, tap neighbor.
- Do not change Group 1 gesture while building Group 2/3.

## Biggest rule: always a playable BOOM

After every start, blast, gravity, and refill:

1. **No free ready match** on the board (kid must swap to score).
2. **≥1 neighbor swap** that creates a valid 3+ match for that level’s rules.

**Never ship a sparse-target board** (too few blues / too few bigs). Colour and size levels use `buildGuaranteedChallengeBoard` — mostly TARGET tiles (~60%+), planted one-swap, randomized (no identical loop). Do not refill with a blocker-only checker.

## Rotate learning each replay (all 3 groups)

Via `beginPlaySession(levelId)`:

- **Colour levels**: rotate target colour; TTS says colour only (`Blue… BOOM!`).
- **Size levels (L4)**: teach by **seeing**, not reading tags.
  - Rotate BIG / TALL / SHORT / SMALL / TINY / FAT / THIN.
  - Board always shows BOTH sides of the pair (tall next to short, fat next to thin).
  - Glyph scale follows **tile size**, not the banner word — never draw every icon as SHORT on a SHORT round.
  - BIG/SMALL → shapes · TALL/SHORT → boy/girl/house/building/chair · TINY → bug/seed/button · FAT/THIN → shape width contrast.
  - Word chips on tiles are optional; voice + visual contrast do the teaching.
- **L1**: progressive shapes; TTS says shape only (`Circle… BOOM!`).
- **L2**: adjective + shape (unchanged style).
- **L6–8**: rotate fruit / veggie / vehicle packs; TTS adjective + name; labels on tiles.
- **L9**: rotate `Blast only VEGETABLES!` ↔ `Blast only FRUITS!`. TTS says category only (`Blast vegetables… BOOM!` / `Blast fruits… BOOM!`) — not each item adjective.
- **L10**: rotate color + category banners (e.g. green vegetables / red fruits).
- **L11**: rotate space/sky pack; TTS object + space fact.
- **L12**: rotate plant-part challenge; TTS plant fact lines.
- **L13**: rotate living ↔ non-living; TTS `Living thing… BOOM!` / `Non living thing… BOOM!`.
- **L14**: rotate solid / liquid / gas; TTS `[Item] is a [State]… BOOM!`.
- **L15**: rotate adjectives ↔ verbs; TTS `[Word] is an Adjective/Verb… BOOM!`.
- **L16**: rotate math targets 10 / 12 / 15 / 20 / 30; TTS `[Equation] is [N]… BOOM!`.

## Match rules

- **none**: same tile id.
- **color**: same colorKey — board mostly that colour.
- **size**: same size — board mostly that size.
- **category**: same fruit/vegetable category — board mostly that category (~65%).
- **colorCategory**: same colorKey + category — board mostly dual targets (~65%).
- **plantPart**: same plant part key — board mostly that part (~65%).
- **living**: living vs non-living — board mostly target side (~65%).
- **matter**: same matter state — board mostly that state (~65%).
- **speechPart**: same part of speech — board mostly adjectives or verbs (~65%).
- **mathTarget**: equation result equals target — board mostly correct equations (~65%).

Ortho row/col ≥3. Score only from the kid’s swap — no auto-cascade.
